  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.0 — SARIF output support.\n\nNew features:\n- SARIF 2.1.0 output format (--format sarif): machine-readable static analysis results consumed natively by GitHub Code Scanning and Azure DevOps, enabling inline PR annotations with zero pipeline scripting\n- Line number detection: each SARIF result now points to the exact line of the unused <PackageReference> element in the .csproj file\n- Multi-project SARIF: scanning a folder emits a single well-formed SARIF document (one run, all findings, all projects listed as artifacts)\n\nUsage:\n  slimdep scan . --format sarif\n  slimdep scan . --format sarif --output results.sarif\n\nBreaking changes: none\n\nv1.0.1 — Patch release.\n- Fixed Supported Features table rendering on NuGet.org (CRLF → LF line endings in README)\n\nv1.0.0 features:\n- Fully-qualified name detection: packages used via Foo.Bar.Type syntax (no using directive) are no longer false-positives\n- .slimdepignore support: add a .slimdepignore file to suppress specific packages from analysis\n- --ignore flag: suppress packages inline without a file (slimdep scan . --ignore Pkg1 --ignore Pkg2)\n- slimdep ignore command: manage .slimdepignore from the CLI (add / remove / list)\n- Central Package Management (CPM) support: GlobalPackageReference entries are automatically excluded\n- XAML namespace analysis: xmlns clr-namespace declarations in .xaml files (WPF, MAUI) are now scanned\n- Razor / CSHTML namespace analysis: @using directives in .razor and .cshtml files (Blazor, MVC) are now scanned\n- Parallel multi-project scanning: all projects scanned concurrently (bounded by CPU count)",
